9
00:38:27,272 --> 00:38:33,272
Doctor Zhivago () is a 1965 epic historical romance film directed by David Lean with a
screenplay by Robert Bolt, based on the 1957 novel by Boris Pasternak.

10
00:42:43,636 --> 00:42:49,636
The story is set in Russia during World War I and the Russian Civil War.

11
00:47:00,000 --> 00:47:06,000
The film stars Omar Sharif in the title role as Yuri Zhivago, a married physician and poet whose life is altered
by the Russian Revolution and subsequent civil war, and Julie Christie as his lover Lara Antipova.

12
00:51:16,363 --> 00:51:22,363
Geraldine Chaplin, Tom Courtenay, Rod Steiger, Alec Guinness, Ralph
Richardson, Siobhán McKenna, and Rita Tushingham play supporting roles.

13
00:55:32,727 --> 00:55:38,727
Although immensely popular in the West, Pasternak's book
was banned in the Soviet Union for decades.

14
00:59:49,090 --> 00:59:55,090
As the film could not be made there, it was instead filmed mostly in Spain.

15
01:04:05,454 --> 01:04:11,454
It was an international co-production between
Metro-Goldwyn-Mayer and Italian producer Carlo Ponti.

16
01:08:21,818 --> 01:08:27,818
Contemporary critics were critical of its length at over three hours and claimed that it trivialized history,
but acknowledged the intensity of the love story and the film's treatment of human themes.

17
01:12:38,181 --> 01:12:44,181
At the 38th Academy Awards, Doctor Zhivago was nominated for ten Oscars (including Best Picture) and won five:
Best Adapted Screenplay, Original Score, Cinematography, Art Direction, and Costume Design.

18
01:16:54,545 --> 01:17:00,545
It also won five awards at the 23rd Golden Globe
Awards including Best Motion Picture.

19
01:21:10,909 --> 01:21:16,909
As of 2022, it is the ninth highest-grossing film
worldwide after adjusting for inflation.

20
01:25:27,272 --> 01:25:33,272
In 1998, it was ranked 39th by the American Film Institute on their 100 Years...

21
01:29:43,636 --> 01:29:49,636
100 Movies list, and by the British Film Institute in 1999
as the 27th greatest British film ever.
